    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53">

                <pb facs="0188" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg54"/>

                <head>No. 53.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Carlisle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 30,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 27.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 44 of October 22
                    last, in which you report the final suppression of the military mutiny at Sucre
                    and the complete restoration of civil order.</p>
                <p>The Department receives this information with satisfaction, and confidently hopes
                    that the restoration of domestic peace will prove auspicious of an era of
                    prosperity and advancement for Bolivia under the benign influence of a stable
                    constitutional government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
